Let's start by multiplying the factors within and without the square roots:

$\begin{align}
6\sqrt{15y^4}\cdot 2\sqrt{20y^2}
&=6\cdot 2\cdot\sqrt{15y^4}\cdot\sqrt{20y^2}
\\\\
&=12\sqrt{300y^6}
\end{align}$

Now we remove all perfect squares from inside the square root:

$\begin{align}
12\sqrt{300y^6}&=12\sqrt{10^2\cdot \left(y^3 \right)^2\cdot3}
\\\\
&=12\sqrt{10^2}\cdot\sqrt{\left(y^3 \right)^2}\cdot\sqrt{3}
\\\\
&=12\cdot 10\cdot y^3\sqrt{3}
\\\\
&=120y^3\sqrt{3}
\end{align}$
